  :adr/body
  "# Context\n\n`kotobase-peer`はDatomic-shaped model、Datalog、Prolly snapshot、novelty chain、fold、Merkle-LSM host、materialized view、S3/R2 adapter、backup/restoreを一つのpeerとして所有してきた。抽出repoは増えたが、production経路は抽出前のcopyを使う箇所が残り、Prolly経路とobject-store Merkle-LSM経路は同じI/O contract上の選択肢でなく別entry pointとして成長した。\n\nさらに『ProllyとMerkle-LSMは二tierの一system』という説明は有力な構成仮説ではあるが、単独Prolly、単独Merkle-LSM、合成profileのコストを同じworkloadで比較する前に結論を固定している。Filecoin/FEVMも、block provider、durable archive、on-chain anchor、query executionのどれを指すかを分けないとhot pathへchain latencyを持ち込む。\n\n# Decision\n\n## D1. 六層を固定する\n\nProduct/API -> Logical Datom model -> Query -> Storage engine -> Persistence contract -> Provider/verificationの一方向依存とする。`datom`、`datom-model`、`datalog`はCID、IPLD、S3、Prolly、Merkle-LSMを知らない。engineはBlockStore/RefStore capabilityだけを知り、provider APIを直接呼ばない。deploymentはengine内部algorithmを持たない。\n\n## D2. engine contractを独立repoにする\n\n`kotoba-lang/kotobase-engine-contract`はIEngine（profile、empty-state、restore-state、transact、open-snapshot、scan、history、checkpoint）、receipt validator、memory correctness oracle、再利用可能conformanceを所有する。semantic conformance、provider crash/concurrency、performanceは別suiteとし、正しいが遅いengineと速いが答えを失うengineを同じPASSにしない。\n\n## D3. identityを三つに割る\n\ntransactionごとの`:tx-root`、checkpoint時のvisible logical Datom集合をcommitする`:logical-checkpoint-root`、Prolly rootまたはMerkle-LSM manifestである`:physical-root`を別fieldにする。異なるengineのphysical CID一致を要求しない。cross-engine equivalenceはtransaction/query/historyの答えとlogical checkpoint rootで判定する。logical rootの全graph再計算をforeground transactionへ入れず、checkpointまたは増分accumulatorで生成する。\n\n## D4. storage profileを競争させる\n\n`:memory`はoracle、`:prolly`、`:merkle-lsm`、`:lsm-prolly-checkpoint`は独立profileである。合成profileは単独経路より優れると実測されるまでdefaultにしない。`prolly-tree`と`merkle-lsm`は汎用物理primitiveを所有し、Datom transaction、tenant、S3を所有しない。engine repoがprimitiveを合成する。\n\n## D5. Filecoin/FEVMはengine外\n\nFilecoinはcheckpoint/run packをPieceCIDへ変換し、upload -> registered -> proving -> verifiedを追う非同期archiveである。FEVMはdatabase-id、epoch、logical checkpoint root、任意のarchive PieceCIDをanchorする。mutable database head、foreground commit、Datalog executionをFEVMへ置かない。Filecoin retrievalを使う場合もCID再検証付きcold restore sourceであり、hot query providerではない。\n\n## D6. 移行はcopy移動よりcontractを先にする\n\n(1) kotobase-peerへの新規責任追加をfreeze (2) contract+memory oracle (3) 既存Prolly経路adapter (4) Merkle-LSM経路adapter (5) shadow writeとlogical equivalence (6) provider/crash/performance qualification (7) default選定 (8) kotobase-peerをfacadeへ縮退、の順とする。production codeを先に移動しない。\n\n# Repository ownership\n\n- datom: representation only\n- datom-model: schema/transact/pull/entity semantics; no persistence\n- datalog: storage-free executor over IPatternSource\n- kotobase-engine-contract: engine seam, receipt, profiles, memory oracle, semantic conformance\n- prolly-tree / merkle-lsm / chain: generic physical primitives\n- kotobase-engine-prolly / future kotobase-engine-lsm: Datom persistence engines\n- kotobase-storage: immutable block/mutable ref/large-object provider contracts\n- provider repos: S3/R2/B2/D1/Postgres/SQLite/IndexedDB implementations\n- archive-filecoin / anchor-fevm: asynchronous durability and anchoring\n- kotobase-server: protocol translation against IEngine\n- net-kotobase: tenant/auth/billing/routing/deployment only\n\n# First landing\n\n`orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-engine-contract` was added locally with zero runtime dependencies. Its conformance proves add/query/retract/as-of/history/idempotent replay/checkpoint against the memory oracle on JVM and ClojureScript. Archive lifecycle explicitly rejects skipping upload/registration/proving, and profile validation rejects Filecoin/FEVM as database storage engines.\n\n# Second landing\n\n`kotobase-engine-prolly` now implements typed EDN round-trip over Arrangement's string primitive, durable manifest restore, persisted idempotency, memory-oracle differential equivalence, and immutable-block-before-CAS publication. JVM and CLJS provider coordinators are separate host interpreters. The CLJS restore trampoline is correctness-only and remains performance-blocked until a direct async cursor replaces restart-on-miss hydration. West registration waits for publishable revisions; generated west.yml is not edited with invented SHAs.\n\n# Consequences\n\nThe split adds an explicit adapter per engine, but removes the implicit requirement that every new physical path enter kotobase-peer. Physical formats may evolve independently while logical equivalence remains testable. FEVM/Filecoin can improve durability and proof without setting the query latency floor. Existing production remains unchanged until an adapter passes the shared semantic and provider-specific gates."
